		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4491&amp;p=33527#p33527"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>So I have the standard charger that comes with a GD-77. I noticed the battery wasn't quite hanging in there like it used to (it's old) but also that the charger would turn red during charging but then after a long while start flashing between red and green. If I leave it alone long enough, it went green, but I figured this must be a sign that my aging battery was on the way out.<br><br>Purchased a brand new replacement battery from Radioddity, but now that battery on its first charge is doing the same thing!<br><br>Is the red/green flashing one of those 90% charged indicators that some Motorola chargers do or is my charger broken?</div></blockquote>The charger base that comes with the GD77 is not very good.  Most people replace the PCB in the charger base with a TP5100 module board<br><br>See the posts on this forum about this modification<br><br><br>e.g.<br><br><a href="https://www.opengd77.com/viewtopic.php?f=7&amp;t=2887&amp;hilit=tp5100" class="postlink">viewtopic.php?f=7&amp;t=2887&amp;hilit=tp5100</a><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Thu Oct 17, 2024 6:56 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
