		<title type="html"><![CDATA[OEM GD-77 Charger likes to blink]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4491&amp;p=33526#p33526"><![CDATA[
So I have the standard charger that comes with a GD-77. I noticed the battery wasn't quite hanging in there like it used to (it's old) but also that the charger would turn red during charging but then after a long while start flashing between red and green. If I leave it alone long enough, it went green, but I figured this must be a sign that my aging battery was on the way out.<br><br>Purchased a brand new replacement battery from Radioddity, but now that battery on its first charge is doing the same thing!<br><br>Is the red/green flashing one of those 90% charged indicators that some Motorola chargers do or is my charger broken?<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=3765">KB0PCH</a> — Thu Oct 17, 2024 6:09 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
